# API Route Conventions

## File Structure

API routes live in `apps/api/pages/api/v1/`. Organize by resource:

```
pages/api/v1/
  users/
    index.ts          -- GET (list), POST (create)
    [id].ts           -- GET (read), PATCH (update), DELETE (delete)
    [id]/
      sessions.ts     -- GET user sessions
  teams/
    index.ts
    [id].ts
    [id]/
      members.ts
```

## Handler Pattern

Every route handler follows this structure:

```typescript
import { withAuth } from "@/lib/middleware/auth";
import { withErrorHandler } from "@/lib/middleware/errors";
import { withRateLimit } from "@/lib/middleware/rate-limit";
import { CreateUserRequest, CreateUserResponse } from "@acme/shared";
import type { NextApiRequest, NextApiResponse } from "next";

async function handler(req: NextApiRequest, res: NextApiResponse) {
  switch (req.method) {
    case "GET":
      return handleGet(req, res);
    case "POST":
      return handlePost(req, res);
    default:
      res.setHeader("Allow", ["GET", "POST"]);
      return res.status(405).json({
        data: null,
        error: { message: "Method not allowed", code: "METHOD_NOT_ALLOWED" },
      });
  }
}

export default withErrorHandler(withAuth(withRateLimit(handler)));
```

## Request Validation

Always validate request bodies and query parameters with Zod schemas from `@acme/shared`:

```typescript
import { CreateUserRequest } from "@acme/shared";

async function handlePost(req: NextApiRequest, res: NextApiResponse) {
  const body = CreateUserRequest.parse(req.body);
  // body is now fully typed and validated
}
```

## Response Envelope

All responses use a consistent envelope:

```typescript
// Success
res.status(200).json({
  data: { id: "usr_123", name: "Alice" },
  error: null,
  meta: { total: 42, page: 1, limit: 20 }, // optional, for paginated responses
});

// Error
res.status(400).json({
  data: null,
  error: { message: "Email is required", code: "VALIDATION_ERROR" },
});
```

## Authentication

- Use `withAuth()` middleware for protected routes.
- Access the authenticated user via `req.user` (added by middleware).
- For public routes, omit `withAuth()` from the wrapper chain.
- For routes needing specific roles: `withAuth({ roles: ["admin"] })`.

## Pagination

List endpoints support cursor-based pagination:

```typescript
const { cursor, limit = 20 } = PaginationParams.parse(req.query);
const results = await userRepo.list({ cursor, limit: limit + 1 });
const hasMore = results.length > limit;
const items = hasMore ? results.slice(0, -1) : results;

res.status(200).json({
  data: items,
  error: null,
  meta: {
    hasMore,
    nextCursor: hasMore ? items[items.length - 1].id : null,
  },
});
```

## Error Codes

Use `AppError` with standard codes:

- `VALIDATION_ERROR` (400) -- invalid input
- `UNAUTHORIZED` (401) -- missing or invalid auth
- `FORBIDDEN` (403) -- insufficient permissions
- `NOT_FOUND` (404) -- resource does not exist
- `CONFLICT` (409) -- duplicate or state conflict
- `RATE_LIMITED` (429) -- too many requests
- `INTERNAL_ERROR` (500) -- unexpected server error
